{
  "id": "walk-up-landing",
  "name": "Nix's Walk-up",
  "description": "The top-floor landing of the old walk-up on the Ribbon where Nix lives, four flights up with no lift. Two-tone walls, green below and cream above, chipped and patched; pipes and wiring along the ceiling under a caged fluorescent tube that buzzes. On the left the stairwell drops away behind a worn wooden rail and a black newel post, its handrail running down past a caged bulb on the wall and a green exit sign above; a mop bucket waits by the rail. Ahead, a tall window with a cracked, taped pane over a radiator looks out on the Ribbon's towers, beside a red fire-hose cabinet. A long worn runner carpet leads down the hall. Her door is deep blue and worn at the handle: a brass plate, two locks, a doormat, a takeout bag on the handle, a potted plant and a stack of flattened delivery boxes, a line of warm light underneath. The neighbour's dark door has slippers on the mat, an umbrella stand and a little shrine with a candle, and TV light flickering under it.",
